  "hypothesis": "H82-CSAM (Coupled Subsurface-to-Surface Up-Dip Advection, Upslope Hydraulic Plume Back-Projection & Biharmonic Basement Flexure with Anisotropic Ridge-Crest Dinkelbach Allocation): Dipping basin-bounding normal faults offset dense/magnetic pre-Tertiary basement and deep 1-5 km conductors in the hanging wall 150-350 m down-dip of the surface rupture, while lateral shallow groundwater flow advects thermal anomalies down-gradient into valleys. Back-projecting CBA/HGM gravity, RTP magnetic HGM, and MT clay-cap edges up-dip along +grad(Basement_15) onto deconfounded surface scarps and back-projecting shallow temperature gradients upslope along +grad(z_smooth), combined with biharmonic basement flexure |nabla^4 B_15|, cross-branch fluvial chi-disequilibrium, transtensional releasing-bend fault-valve dilation, and multi-scale potential-field tilt-phase congruency inside a strictly Leave-One-Quadrant-Out (LOQO) 114-channel ensemble + Dinkelbach 300 m submodular emitter, recovers concealed range-front piedmont and intra-basin faults missed by USGS/INGENIOUS.",
  "mechanism": "106 static zero-SGMC physical channels (98 base + 8 novel H82-CSAM up-dip/upslope/flexure/chi/phase channels) + 8 fold-visible structural continuation channels + 8 geomechanical-CSAM interaction channels fitted via strictly Leave-One-Quadrant-Out (LOQO) spatial cross-fitting with Horvitz-Thompson 4-stratum inverse-probability weighting, across-strike 1D Hessian ridge-crest sharpening, and exact Bayes-calibrated Dinkelbach 300 m submodular dot placement under a simultaneous 168-raster 3.0-px halo overlap cap (0.610 <= 0.70).",
  "named_non_fault_mimic_process": "Alluvial fan coalescent aprons, shoreline beach ridges (Lake Lahontan), and non-tectonic volcanic flow-front / caldera margins in low-slope basins, plus 1 m LiDAR tile-boundary step artifacts and unfaulted steep canyon talus slopes.",
  "deconfounding_strategy": "(1) Up-dip basement advection requires spatial coincidence between the up-dip-advected subsurface gravity/magnetic/MT step and a deconfounded surface scarp; (2) within-survey quantile normalization on acquisition_block_id_100m.tif and explicit lidar_1m_tile_boundary_dist_km conditioning suppress survey-seam steps; (3) strike-frame tangential vs normal gradient projection vetoes drainage canyons perpendicular to structural strike.",
